---
/**
 * The coverage dashboard.
 *
 * What the corpus covers today, what it does not, and what a reviewer has to
 * settle next. Every number here comes from the topic map, and the map
 * records the terms that produced each link, so any claim on this page can
 * be checked against the corpus.
 *
 * This page is deliberately a map, not a promise. A topic with questions is
 * not a topic a learner has mastered.
 */
import Site from '../../layouts/Site.astro';
import delta from '../../../docs/phases/07-expansion/coverage-delta.json';
import {
  bandLabel,
  coverage,
  coverageSummary,
  reviewQueue,
  subjectCoverage,
  topicStatuses,
  type CoverageBand,
} from '../../lib/coverage';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '') + '/';
const summary = coverageSummary();
const subjects = subjectCoverage();
const statuses = topicStatuses();
const queue = reviewQueue();

const bySubject = new Map<string, typeof statuses>();
const sign = (value: number) => (value >= 0 ? `+${value}` : `${value}`);
for (const status of statuses) {
  const list = bySubject.get(status.topic.subjectId) ?? [];
  list.push(status);
  bySubject.set(status.topic.subjectId, list);
}
---

<Site
  title="Coverage"
  active="coverage"
  description="Which syllabus topics the JELET corpus covers, which it does not, and what a reviewer should settle next."
>
  <div class="page-intro">
    <p class="eyebrow">SYLLABUS COVERAGE</p>
    <h1>What the corpus covers.</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      {coverage.edition}, bulletin of {coverage.bulletinDate}. {summary.topics} topics across four subjects,
      mapped against {coverage.mappedQuestions} corpus questions. Every link records the terms that produced
      it, so any number here can be checked against the corpus.
    </p>
  </div>

  <section class="card" style="margin-bottom:1.4rem" aria-labelledby="headline-heading">
    <h2 id="headline-heading" style="font-size:1.15rem">The shape of it</h2>
    <div class="stat-grid">
      <div class="stat"><b>{summary.covered} of {summary.topics}</b><span>Topics with a markable question</span><em>{summary.topicCoverage}% of the syllabus</em></div>
      <div class="stat"><b>{summary.broad}</b><span>Broadly covered</span><em>8 or more questions across 3 or more papers</em></div>
      <div class="stat"><b>{summary.thin + summary.moderate}</b><span>Partly covered</span><em>too few questions, or too few papers</em></div>
      <div class="stat"><b>{summary.none}</b><span>Not covered</span><em>no markable question at all</em></div>
    </div>
    <div class="table" role="table" style="margin-top:1rem">
      <div role="row"><b role="cell">Questions mapped to a topic</b><span role="cell">{coverage.mappedQuestions}</span></div>
      <div role="row"><b role="cell">In a syllabus subject but not yet mapped</b><span role="cell">{coverage.unmappedQuestions} — these are in the review queue</span></div>
      <div role="row"><b role="cell">Matched two topics equally well</b><span role="cell">{coverage.conflictCount} — a reviewer decides these, not the script</span></div>
      <div role="row"><b role="cell">Outside the 2026 syllabus</b><span role="cell">{coverage.outsideSyllabusQuestions} — the Fundamentals of Computers section the older papers carried and the syllabus no longer lists</span></div>
    </div>
    <p class="micro" style="margin-top:.8rem">
      Coverage is a count of questions and papers. It is not a claim that a learner has mastered a topic,
      and no number here predicts a score.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="card" style="margin-bottom:1.4rem" aria-labelledby="delta-heading">
    <div class="section-head">
      <h2 id="delta-heading" style="font-size:1.15rem">What changed in Phase 07</h2>
      <span class="micro">measured against the map as it stood at the start of the phase</span>
    </div>
    <div class="stat-grid">
      <div class="stat">
        <b>{delta.currentSummary.covered} of {delta.currentSummary.topics}</b>
        <span>Topics with a markable question</span>
        <em>{sign(delta.delta.topicsCovered)} on the {delta.baselineSummary.covered} covered before</em>
      </div>
      <div class="stat">
        <b>{delta.currentSummary.mappedQuestions}</b>
        <span>Questions mapped to a topic</span>
        <em>{sign(delta.delta.questionsMapped)} on the {delta.baselineSummary.mappedQuestions} mapped before</em>
      </div>
      <div class="stat">
        <b>{delta.currentSummary.broad + delta.currentSummary.moderate}</b>
        <span>Topics with real range</span>
        <em>{sign(delta.delta.broadTopics + delta.delta.moderateTopics)} on the {delta.baselineSummary.broad + delta.baselineSummary.moderate} before</em>
      </div>
      <div class="stat">
        <b>{delta.currentSummary.conflicts}</b>
        <span>Ties left for a reviewer</span>
        <em>{delta.baselineSummary.conflicts} before, all of them resolved</em>
      </div>
    </div>
    {delta.newlyCovered.length > 0 && (
      <>
        <p class="micro" style="margin-top:1rem">Topics that went from no markable question to some:</p>
        <ul class="micro" style="margin:.3rem 0 0;padding-left:1.1rem">
          {delta.newlyCovered.map((topic) => (
            <li>{topic.name} — {topic.questions} question{topic.questions === 1 ? '' : 's'}, now {bandLabel(topic.band as CoverageBand).toLowerCase()}</li>
          ))}
        </ul>
      </>
    )}
    {delta.stillUncovered.length > 0 && (
      <>
        <p class="micro" style="margin-top:1rem">Topics still with no markable question, and why:</p>
        <ul class="micro" style="margin:.3rem 0 0;padding-left:1.1rem">
          {delta.stillUncovered.map((topic) => (
            <li><b>{topic.name}</b> — {topic.reason}</li>
          ))}
        </ul>
      </>
    )}
    <p class="micro" style="margin-top:.8rem">
      The baseline is rebuilt from the term lists as they stood at the start of the phase, and those lists
      reproduce the recorded starting figures exactly, so the comparison is between two real maps rather
      than between a map and a note.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="card" style="margin-bottom:1.4rem" aria-labelledby="subjects-heading">
    <h2 id="subjects-heading" style="font-size:1.15rem">By subject</h2>
    <div class="table" role="table">
      {subjects.map((subject) => (
        <div role="row">
          <b role="cell">{subject.name}</b>
          <span role="cell">
            {subject.covered} of {subject.topics} topics covered · {subject.broad} broad, {subject.moderate} moderate,
            {' '}{subject.thin} thin, {subject.none} not covered · {subject.questions} markable questions, {subject.marks} marks
          </span>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  {subjects.map((subject) => (
    <section class="card" style="margin-bottom:1.4rem" aria-labelledby={`subject-${subject.id}`}>
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2 id={`subject-${subject.id}`} style="font-size:1.15rem">{subject.name}</h2>
        <span class="micro">{subject.covered} of {subject.topics} topics covered</span>
      </div>
      <div class="stack">
        {(bySubject.get(subject.id) ?? []).map((status) => (
          <details class="card-flat coverage-topic" data-topic={status.topic.id} data-band={status.band}>
            <summary>
              <span class="coverage-code">{status.topic.code}</span>
              <span class="coverage-name">{status.topic.name}</span>
              <span class={`pill coverage-band ${status.band}`}>{bandLabel(status.band)}</span>
              <span class="micro">{status.topic.coveredQuestions} questions · {status.topic.coveredYears} papers</span>
            </summary>
            <div class="details-body">
              <p class="micro">{status.topic.detail}</p>
              <p class="micro"><strong>{status.note}</strong></p>
              {status.topic.questions.length > 0 && (
                <ul class="micro" style="margin:.4rem 0 0;padding-left:1.1rem">
                  {status.topic.questions.slice(0, 12).map((question) => (
                    <li>
                      <a href={`${base}library/${question.paperId}/#q${question.n}`}>
                        {question.year} Q{question.n}
                      </a>
                      {question.held ? ' · held' : question.voided ? ' · voided by the board' : ''}
                      {' '}· matched on {question.terms.join(', ')}
                    </li>
                  ))}
                  {status.topic.questions.length > 12 && (
                    <li class="micro">…and {status.topic.questions.length - 12} more.</li>
                  )}
                </ul>
              )}
            </div>
          </details>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>
  ))}

  <section class="card" style="margin-bottom:1.4rem" aria-labelledby="queue-heading">
    <div class="section-head">
      <h2 id="queue-heading" style="font-size:1.15rem">What a reviewer settles next</h2>
      <span class="micro">{queue.length} items</span>
    </div>
    <p class="small" style="color:var(--muted)">
      These are the decisions the script refuses to make on its own: a question that two topics claim, a
      question no topic claims, and a topic with no markable coverage at all.
    </p>
    <div class="table-wrap">
      <table class="table" data-review-queue>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col">Kind</th>
            <th scope="col">Subject</th>
            <th scope="col">Item</th>
            <th scope="col">What has to be settled</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {queue.slice(0, 60).map((item) => (
            <tr data-queue-kind={item.kind}>
              <td>{item.kind === 'conflict' ? 'Tie' : item.kind === 'uncovered-topic' ? 'Gap' : 'Unmapped'}</td>
              <td>{item.subject}</td>
              <td><a href={item.link}>{item.reference}</a></td>
              <td class="small">{item.detail}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    {queue.length > 60 && <p class="micro" style="margin-top:.6rem">…and {queue.length - 60} more in the queue file.</p>}
  </section>

  <section class="card" aria-labelledby="limits-heading">
    <h2 id="limits-heading" style="font-size:1.15rem">What this page does not say</h2>
    <ul class="small" style="color:var(--muted)">
      <li>It does not claim a topic is understood because questions exist for it. A learner may have met a topic once.</li>
      <li>It does not measure difficulty. A question can be mapped and still be the hardest in the paper.</li>
      <li>It does not claim any learning path works. The mapping says what is in the corpus, not what a learner should do next.</li>
      <li>It does not extrapolate. The 258 questions in the section the 2026 syllabus dropped are counted separately rather than folded in.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</Site>
